      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) that makes the seven-digit number \\( 854n526 \\) divisible by 11, we can use the divisibility rule for 11. According to this rule, a number is divisible by 11 if the difference between the sum of the digits in the odd positions and the sum of the digits in the even positions is a multiple of 11 (including 0).\n\nHere is the step-by-step reasoning and calculation:\n\n1. Identify the digits in the odd and even positions of the number \\( 854n526 \\).\n   - Digits in the odd positions: 8, 4, 5, 6\n   - Digits in the even positions: 5, n, 2\n\n2. Calculate the sum of the digits in the odd positions.\n   \\[\n   8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 23\n   \\]\n3. Calculate the sum of the digits in the even positions.\n   \\[\n   5 + n + 2\n   \\]\n4. Set up the equation based on the divisibility rule. The difference between the sum of the digits in the odd positions and the sum of the digits in the even positions must be a multiple of 11.\n   \\[\n   23 - (5 + n + 2) \\equiv 0 \\pmod{11}\n   \\]\n   Simplify the left side of the congruence:\n   \\[\n   23 - 7 - n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{11}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   16 - n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{11}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n \\equiv 16 \\pmod{11}\n   \\]\n   Since \\( n \\) is a digit (0 through 9), we need to find the equivalent digit in the range 0 to 9. The equivalent value of 16 modulo 11 is:\n   \\[\n   n = 16 - 11 = 5\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( n \\) that makes the number \\( 854n526 \\) divisible by 11 is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
